---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import books from '../../books.json';

const total = books.length;
---

<Base
  title="About — Nimble Reads"
  description="Nimble Reads is a proven method for reading the world's most important books efficiently."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      Nimble Reads is a proven method for working through the world's most
      important books efficiently. It is intended for readers of serious
      intellectual ambition who have concluded, correctly, that their present
      rate of progress is inadequate.
    </p>

    <p>
      The canon is larger than any individual can read, and most reading
      capacity is lost before a book is opened — spent on titles selected by
      proximity rather than merit, and on the indefinite deferral that follows
      when a reading list arrives without an order of priority. Nimble Reads
      treats reading as an allocation problem: {total} works ranked by
      measurable standing rather than editorial preference, enough of each to
      establish its relevance before an evening is committed to it, and a record
      of what has been completed. Attention is finite. It should be budgeted
      accordingly.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
